WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.630
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.160
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.630
between Subway in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.003
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.490
At Subway in the UK,

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.765
you can get sandwiches
in four different sizes.

00:00:18.975 --> 00:00:21.183
Firstly, we have toasted bites,

00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:24.335
a 6-inch sub,

00:00:24.335 --> 00:00:26.185
a foot-long sub,

00:00:27.643 --> 00:00:28.659
and then

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:32.350
you can get a platter.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.050
Joe Avella: And in the
US, we have three sizes.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.343
The 6-inch.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.026
The foot-long.

00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:42.978
There you go.

00:00:42.978 --> 00:00:45.141
For you and your team,

00:00:45.141 --> 00:00:47.415
[grunts] the big boy.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:49.690
Party platter.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.600
The old Subway platypus.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.630
Harry: Now, in the UK, a
platter looks like this.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.310
What they do is they make
four foot-long sandwiches,

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.120
then they cut those into fours.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.290
So you're left with 16 pieces,

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.700
each of which is 3 inches.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.241
Joe: And for the party platter here,

00:01:04.241 --> 00:01:05.682
they take five sandwiches,

00:01:05.682 --> 00:01:07.420
cutting them into three pieces,

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.560
giving you 15 sandwiches total.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.875
In addition, in the US
you can also get yourself

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:15.933
a 3-foot-long party sub.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:17.524
[laughs]

00:01:17.524 --> 00:01:18.960
Look at this thing!

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.740
This is ridiculous.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:24.754
3 feet, so that is, what that's in...

00:01:24.754 --> 00:01:25.870
what do you got in the UK?

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.786
That's...17 meters?

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.643
I have no idea.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.920
Yeah!

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.520
Harry: Now, in the UK, drinks
at Subway come in two sizes.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.690
We have a regular, which
is 400 milliliters.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.650
Joe: 20-ounce Sprite. What up?

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.250
Harry: And we have a large.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.780
Joe: 30-ounce. Boom.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.163
And if you're really thirsty,

00:01:48.163 --> 00:01:49.673
[laughs]

00:01:49.673 --> 00:01:53.032
40 ounces of soda.

00:01:53.032 --> 00:01:56.083
40 ounces is a little
over three cans of soda.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.853
That is way too much soda.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.662
It is way too, that's just too much.

00:02:02.662 --> 00:02:03.952
Harry: If you're a fan
of Subway's cookies,

00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:06.381
in the UK those come in three sizes.

00:02:07.423 --> 00:02:08.473
One cookie.

00:02:11.677 --> 00:02:12.943
Three cookies.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.313
Or 12 cookies.

00:02:17.677 --> 00:02:20.893
Joe: In the US Subway, you
can get a single cookie,

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.853
a dozen cookies,

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:26.570
right like that,

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:27.761
or

00:02:29.336 --> 00:02:30.661
the [laughs]

00:02:30.661 --> 00:02:32.402
hang on, keep rolling,

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:37.170
the 36-cookie platter!

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.978
Booyah!

00:02:38.978 --> 00:02:40.553
[laughs]

00:02:40.553 --> 00:02:42.643
I'm like in Vegas, baby! All in.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.940
Harry: We wanna make
sure that you're getting

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.040
the same amount of filling
as you do in the US

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.170
here in the UK.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.170
So, what we've got here
is a foot-long Italian BMT

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.636
on hearty Italian

00:02:52.636 --> 00:02:54.460
with lettuce and olives.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.068
We're gonna weigh it to
see if the quantities

00:02:56.068 --> 00:02:57.493
are the same.

00:02:57.493 --> 00:02:59.234
Joe: All right, BMT.

00:03:03.093 --> 00:03:03.926
Stay.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.750
Harry: So, the weights are pretty similar.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.180
What we're gonna do is take them apart

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.188
and see how it all adds up.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.420
So, when it comes to the
amount of filling that you get

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.240
in your subs, it looks
like the UK and the US

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.740
are actually pretty identical.

00:03:25.165 --> 00:03:26.570
So, what about calories?

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.410
We found out that the
most popular sub at Subway

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.290
is actually the turkey breast sub.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.130
So if you were to walk into a UK Subway

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.270
and order a regular turkey breast sub

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.510
and then make it a meal by
including a regular drink

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.840
and a cookie, you'd be
looking at 621 calories.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.740
Joe: That same order in
the US is 690 calories.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:45.990
Now, the sub itself is actually

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.950
less calories. It's only 250.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.807
But the drink, the medium
Coke, is around 240,

00:03:50.807 --> 00:03:52.738
and the cookie is 200 calories.

00:03:52.738 --> 00:03:54.580
But wait! According to the internet,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.780
in the US the default actually
comes with two cookies,

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.460
which brings it to a grand
total of 890 calories.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.220
Harry: What about the
calories in another sub?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.910
Well, in the UK, 6 inches
of meatball marinara

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.360
comes in at 492 calories.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.310
Joe: In the US, 6-inch meatball

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.335
is only 430 calories.

00:04:13.335 --> 00:04:14.520
Yo.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.380
Harry: Now, because we're
not sure why our meatball sub

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.120
is more calorific, we're
actually gonna do another test.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.420
We're gonna bring back
our friend the scales.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.009
And we're gonna weigh a meatball.

00:04:25.118 --> 00:04:26.780
Just...

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:27.788
clean that bit.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:29.683
Delicious.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:31.423
Boom.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.510
Joe: And now I will
also weigh one meatball.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.090
Gonna find a good one.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.390
Don't want the sauce to
throw off these measurements.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.160
Get in real close. Get
in real close over there.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.720
Ready? You close?

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.630
Close? Here we go.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.000
Drumroll.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.341
And...uh!

00:04:51.341 --> 00:04:52.620
How much is it?

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.736
No change?

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.370
Our scale is not very accurate. Sorry.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.493
Let's get that weight up on the screen!

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.580
Harry: Unfortunately, Subway in the UK

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.350
doesn't disclose the
full ingredients list.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:07.450
However, there are some things

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.200
we can glean from the website.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.920
In the UK, the ham,
turkey breast, and steak

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.370
that you'll find in your
sandwiches are actually "formed."

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.060
Joe: The turkey bologna
and the turkey salami

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.610
are also made by a process known as

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.493
mechanically separated turkey.

00:05:21.748 --> 00:05:26.748
[typing]
"Mechanically separated

00:05:26.748 --> 00:05:28.487
turkey."

00:05:28.487 --> 00:05:29.904
What do we got here?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.510
Harry: From the allergens list in the UK,

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.840
we can also see that our
meatballs contain milk,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.810
although it's not clear if
the meatballs contain the milk

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.760
or if it just comes
with cheese by default.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.040
Joe: We do have the ingredients list

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.610
of the meatball sandwich at Subway,

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.060
and I'll read that to you right now.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.000
Oh, boy.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.140
Beef, water, breadcrumbs,

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.300
and then we have the
kind of square brackets,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.600
[toasted wheat crumbs,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.691
and now we have the curved brackets,

00:05:54.691 --> 00:05:56.013
(enriched wheat flour,

00:05:56.013 --> 00:05:57.735
now we have the fancy brackets,

00:05:57.735 --> 00:05:59.776
{wheat flour, niacin, reduced iron,

00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:02.150
thiamine mononitrate,

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.091
riboflavin, folic acid},

00:06:04.091 --> 00:06:05.600
close fancy brackets,

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.430
sugar, salt, soybean oil, yeast)],

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.560
and then close the other two brackets.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.393
[clears throat]

00:06:10.393 --> 00:06:13.060
Textured soy protein
concentrate, seasoning,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.670
open brackets again,

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.410
(dehydrated onion and
garlic, salt, spices,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.460
dehydrated parsley, soybean
oil), close brackets,

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.614
soy protein concentrate,
and Romano cheese.

00:06:23.614 --> 00:06:25.110
Can you scroll up, please?

00:06:26.184 --> 00:06:28.100
Keep going. Keep going.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.030
The Romano cheese,

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.888
which is made from pasteurized
"part-skin" cow's milk.

00:06:31.888 --> 00:06:35.570
[sighs] I'm assuming
it's "skim" cow's milk.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:36.670
But to be honest, if I told you

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:39.050
there was cow skin in this
food, would you be surprised?

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:41.620
Part-skim cow's milk,

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.667
cheese cultures, salts, and enzymes.

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.180
"Which enzymes?" you ask.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.440
They're not at liberty to say,

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.280
but rest assured there are enzymes.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.330
Now, on the bright side, the
dough is pretty much normal.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.660
For the classic Italian bread,

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.400
the ingredients are enriched flour,

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.850
which is wheat flour,
niacin, reduced iron,

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.200
thiamine mononitrate,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.349
nitrate? Yeah. OK.

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:00.020
Riboflavin, folic acid,

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.561
water, yeast, sugar,

00:07:01.561 --> 00:07:04.061
soybean oil, salt, wheat gluten,

00:07:04.061 --> 00:07:05.600
cultured wheat flour,

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.016
malted barley flour,

00:07:07.016 --> 00:07:08.791
sunflower lechithin.

00:07:08.791 --> 00:07:10.008
Lecithin.

00:07:10.008 --> 00:07:11.533
Leckithin?

00:07:11.533 --> 00:07:13.010
Hey, did you hear that?

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.570
Phone: Lecithin.
Joe: Lecithin!

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:16.820
Sunflower lecithin, dough conditioner,

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.453
which also has enzymes.

00:07:18.453 --> 00:07:19.611
Which ones, you don't know.

00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:20.812
And ascorbic acid.

00:07:20.812 --> 00:07:22.997
[sighs] All that stuff.

00:07:22.997 --> 00:07:24.447
Harry: While we might not
have an ingredients list

00:07:24.447 --> 00:07:25.413
for our bread, we do know

00:07:25.413 --> 00:07:27.200
that it's likely to not be perfect.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.510
For example, an Irish
court recently declared

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.760
that Subway cannot call its loaves "bread"

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.250
due to the high sugar content.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.663
Subway uses more than
10% sugar in their flour.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.820
Here's everything you
can only find on the menu

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:42.130
at a UK Subway.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.270
So, let's start with the subs.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.520
Now, there are a few kind of default subs

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.930
that you can only find in the UK.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.850
So then once you've chosen
your sub and your bread,

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.720
we've also got a few other
customization options

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.310
that are exclusive to the UK.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.800
For example, in this sub we've
combined a bunch of them.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.380
So, I've gone for chicken tikka.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.960
It has hash browns.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.450
It has sweet corn.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.800
It has vegan garlic aioli.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.825
It has HP brown sauce,

00:08:05.825 --> 00:08:07.400
and it has whole-grain mustard.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.100
So, brown sauce is kind of

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.130
a traditional British condiment.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.888
The biggest brand manufacturer of it

00:08:12.888 --> 00:08:14.450
is a brand called HP,

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.125
which stands for Houses of Parliament,

00:08:16.125 --> 00:08:17.110
to maybe give a nod --

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.840
Joe: Harry, are you really
Brit-splaining to me HP sauce?

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.290
I love HP sauce.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.563
I've been having HP sauce,

00:08:24.563 --> 00:08:26.190
I've had a bottle of HP sauce in my fridge

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.000
for at least the past 20 years.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.266
Harry: Over here, we have the

00:08:29.266 --> 00:08:31.224
meatless meatball marinara sub

00:08:31.224 --> 00:08:34.120
with some vegan
"mozzarella" cheese as well.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.900
And it's on chili paprika bread.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.910
Joe: Our exclusive
customizations in the US

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.550
include avocado, pepper
jack cheese, provolone,

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.880
Swiss cheese, and banana peppers.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:43.990
And if you like your sauce,

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.116
you can make your sauce --

00:08:45.116 --> 00:08:45.949
[laughs]

00:08:45.949 --> 00:08:47.260
If you like a saucy sub,

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.890
you can have the sauciest Subway saucy sub

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.390
here in the United Sauce,

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.850
because we have all these sauces,

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.310
including a balsamic sub
sauce, a creamy sriracha,

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.440
a deli brown mustard, yellow mustard,

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.420
you guys don't have yellow mustard?

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.190
That can't be right.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.370
Sorry if you don't have yellow mustard.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.330
I thought that was everywhere.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.460
Oil.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.560
Oil?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.470
You guys don't have oil either?

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.880
OK.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.821
Subway herb and garlic oil,

00:09:12.821 --> 00:09:14.954
ranch, red wine vinaigrette,

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:18.300
and a special "sub" spice.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.980
Harry: So, moving the subs
to one side for a second,

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.830
we also have some side dishes

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.740
which are exclusive to the UK.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:25.670
Let's start with this,

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.470
which kind of surprised me
when I saw it on the menu,

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.620
but you can actually just get

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.900
a cup of meatballs from Subway.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.460
Next we have the garlic cheesy bread,

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:38.100
which I think is just half of
their hearty Italian 6-inch

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.860
with some garlic butter on it,

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.340
and then they kind of
sprinkle some cheese on top

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.100
and throw it in the toaster oven.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.860
The last side dish is nachos.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.176
They actually just get some Doritos,

00:09:48.176 --> 00:09:49.734
throw them into a box,

00:09:49.734 --> 00:09:52.290
give you some cheese, some jalapeños.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.070
Joe: That is an insult to nachos.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.070
Those are the kind of
nachos you make in your 20s

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.630
when you're drunk at 2 in the morning.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.300
Chips, cheese, microwave
it, throw on some salsa.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:05.250
That is the most depressing
plate of nachos I've ever seen.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.933
That is the worst thing associated,

00:10:07.933 --> 00:10:10.650
excuse me, that is the second-worst thing

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.900
associated with the Subway franchise.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.670
The only exclusive side that you can get

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.510
at a Subway in the US
is the applesauce pouch,

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.230
which we don't have.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.300
Unfortunately, the two Subways we went to

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.770
did not have them available.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:27.260
Can we get a graphic
of the applesauce pouch

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.910
on the screen somewhere near my head?

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.742
Yeah, it looks like that.

00:10:30.742 --> 00:10:32.940
Harry: Now, we wanted to
get as many UK exclusives

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.160
into one sub as possible.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.860
So this is my creation.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.844
I'll be clear, this is not my usual order.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.490
You get the tang of the brown sauce

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:56.507
with the little popping
sweetness of the sweet corn.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:58.774
And then I just got, like, a whole

00:10:58.774 --> 00:11:00.332
hash brown in there as well.

00:11:00.332 --> 00:11:02.350
Do not order the UK Only sub.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:05.240
Joe: And of course, we put together a sub

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.240
with all the USA-only ingredients,

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.650
which is a foot-long barbecue rib sandwich

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:12.430
with the jalapeño
cheddar bread and avocado

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.890
and pepper jack cheese
and provolone cheese

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.010
and Swiss cheese and banana peppers.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.710
Ugh, the US with banana peppers.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.140
I don't know what our thing
is with banana peppers.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:22.670
I'm not into banana peppers.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.079
I don't know why they're so popular here.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.570
That's actually pretty good.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:34.600
I actually like that.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.310
The jalapeño bread. Wow!

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.130
Oh, man, the sriracha sauce.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.350
Ooh, and the avocado.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.100
Whoa, it's got some heat to it, too.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.433
I'm totally surprised.
I kind of like that.

00:11:49.423 --> 00:11:50.544
Yeah!

